<?xml version="1.0"?>
<package >
	<metadata>
		<id>Xrm.Sdk.PluginRegistration</id>
		<version>1.0.0</version>
		<title>Plugin Registration for XrmToolBox</title>
		<authors>Microsoft, Alexey, Jonas, Imran and the Power Platform community</authors>
		<owners>imranakram</owners>
		<iconUrl>https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/13014005/80118859-41d95f80-8589-11ea-9262-8d18cbccbe0c.png</iconUrl>
		<icon>icon.png</icon>
		<readme>docs\README.md</readme>
		<projectUrl>https://github.com/imranakram/PluginRegistration</projectUrl>
		<license type="expression">MIT</license>
		<requireLicenseAcceptance>false</requireLicenseAcceptance>
		<description>
			The Classic Microsoft Dynamics CRM tool, now in the XrmToolBox suite.

			This is special flavor of classical Plugin Registration Tool provided by Microsoft as CRM SDK code sample. It was adopted to the format of an XrmToolBox tool and intended to work with the same set of the Common Data Service / Dynamics 365 / CRM versions as supported by main application.
		</description>
		<summary>The Classic Microsoft Dynamics CRM tool, now in the XrmToolBox suite</summary>
		<releaseNotes>
New: Custom APIs
- #173: Register, edit and delete Custom APIs together with their request parameters and response properties, from the Register menu or an API's context menu. Fields that Dataverse fixes after creation are read-only, and managed APIs are protected (thanks @WebbontheWeb)
- #173: Display by Message lists every Custom API, also those without steps, with the steps on its message beneath it
- #173: A new API is created in an unmanaged solution that you pick or create, with the publisher prefix applied to its unique name. Parameters added later join the solutions the API is in
- #173: Add to Solution adds an API with all its parameters and properties in one go
- #173: Steps can be registered and edited on private Custom APIs

New: managed identities (Dataverse online only)
- Link a managed identity to a plug-in assembly or package from its context menu or the toolbar, and create, edit or delete identities from the same dialog. New identities use version 2, which Microsoft recommends. Based on Plugin Identity Manager by David Rivard (https://github.com/drivardxrm/Driv.XTB.PluginIdentityManager), with thanks
- The properties pane shows the linked identity of an assembly or package

UX &amp; stability improvements, bug fixes
- #175: Each connection now shows its own SDK messages. After changing connection, or with the tool open in two tabs, the step editor used to offer the messages of the first environment (thanks @WebbontheWeb)
- #175: Refresh (F5) retries a failed load, and a failed refresh keeps the current tree instead of closing the connection
- #175: Registration commands are disabled while the organization is loading
- #175: Editing a step whose message isn't available, such as a private message, explains why instead of failing
- #148: Creating or updating a plug-in package shows a wait cursor and locks the dialog until the upload has finished
- #15: Unregistering shows a wait cursor, and the progress bar in the XrmToolBox status bar now advances with the work
- Unregistering runs in the background behind the XrmToolBox wait box, which shows how far it has got, so XrmToolBox no longer freezes on an assembly with many plug-ins. If a delete fails partway, the tree is reloaded to show what is left
- An assembly or plug-in that is part of a plug-in package can no longer be unregistered on its own. Dataverse deleted its plug-in types and only then refused to delete the assembly; the tool now refuses before anything is deleted
- The plug-in package dialog shows the XrmToolBox wait box while it registers or updates a package
- #100: Editing a webhook keeps its header, query string or key values when you leave them empty. Dataverse never returns them, so the dialog now says so instead of showing an empty list. Values with quotes, &amp; or &lt; are saved correctly

Security
- #178: Removed the unused System.Security.Cryptography.Pkcs reference, which had two denial-of-service advisories (GHSA-846f-f764-76mx, GHSA-2fmv-rv2c-59x7)
		</releaseNotes>

		<tags>XrmToolBox Plugins PluginRegistration</tags>
		<dependencies>
			<dependency id="XrmToolBoxPackage" version="1.2025.10.74" />
			<dependency id="CsvHelper" version="33.1.0"/>
			<dependency id="EPPlus" version="8.4.1"/>
			<dependency id="EPPlus.System.Drawing" version="8.4.0"/>
		</dependencies>
	</metadata>
